      "description": "If your server enforces AUTH_TOKEN, paste it here. Leave blank for unauthenticated local dev.",
      "required": false
    }
  ],
  "overviewMarkdown": "## Adaptive Memory Engine — HTTP variant\n\nPersistent, searchable long-term memory for every AI in TypingMind. **No Node.js required** — works on any browser, any device.\n\n- **23 tools** via HTTP Action — store, search, recall, ask, version history, suggestions, dedup, export\n- **Knowledge graph** — built-in, automatic\n- **Multi-model memory** — works across GPT, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek, Grok, Mistral\n- **Self-hosted** — your data, your server, your OpenAI key\n- **Free** — no subscription\n\n**When to use HTTP instead of MCP**: install this variant if `npx` is not available on your machine. The MCP variant (`plugin.json` at the repo root) is otherwise functionally identical and more efficient.\n\n**How to use**:\n- *\"Remember I prefer dark roast coffee\"* → saves\n- *\"What do you remember about my project?\"* → recalls\n- *\"Show my memory version history\"* → restores prior versions\n- *\"Import my ChatGPT history from /path/to/conversations.json\"* → bulk import\n\nMemory lives at `{mcpServerUrl}/api/tools/{tool_name}` — every tool is a single POST endpoint.\n\n**Note on arrays**: tag arrays are passed as **comma-separated strings** (e.g. `work,personal`). The AI will pass them in plain English.",
  "authenticationType": "AUTH_TYPE_NONE",
  "dynamicContextEndpoints": [
    {
      "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
      "name": "How to use this plugin",
      "url": "",
      "method": "GET",
      "source": "static",
      "staticContent": "You have access to the Adaptive Memory Engine via HTTP. Use store_memory proactively when the user mentions a preference, decision, or fact worth remembering. Use search_memories / ask_memory BEFORE answering questions that may relate to past context. Use list_suggestions weekly to review duplicates. Use export_memories with format='csv' for portability. Tag arrays are passed as comma-separated strings (e.g. 'work,personal').",
      "cacheDurationHours": 24,
      "cacheRefreshPolicy": "REFRESH_NEVER"
    }
  ],
  "pluginFunctions": [
    {
      "id": "bbb01111-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbb1",
      "name": "store_memory",
      "implementationType": "http",
      "httpAction": {
        "id": "ha01111-ha01-4a01-8a01-haaaaaaaaa1",
        "url": "{mcpServerUrl}/api/tools/store_memory",
        "method": "POST",
        "hasBody": true,
        "hasHeaders": true,
        "requestBody": "{\"arguments\": {\"key\": \"{key}\", \"content\": \"{content}\", \"tags_csv\": \"{tags}\", \"auto_tag\": {auto_tag}}}",
        "requestHeaders": "{\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}",
        "requestBodyFormat": "json"
      },
      "openaiSpec": {
        "name": "store_memory",
        "description": "Save content to long-term memory with automatic embeddings and optional AI auto-tagging. Use whenever the user expresses a preference, decision, project fact, or any detail worth remembering across sessions.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["key", "content"],
          "properties": {
            "key": {"type": "string", "description": "Short stable identifier for the memory (e.g. 'user-coffee-preference')"},
            "content": {"type": "string", "description": "The fact to remember in plain English"},
            "tags": {"type": "string", "description": "Comma-separated tags (e.g. 'work,personal')"},
            "auto_tag": {"type": "boolean", "description": "If true, ask the AI to suggest relevant tags"}
          }
        }
      },
      "outputType": "respond_to_ai"
    },
